    {
      "id": "p0149-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "As we've seen, English words appear all the time in Japanese games. Over the years, these English words have formed a limited \"English game vocabulary\" that Japanese gamers naturally absorb. However, it's still common for English phrases to be simplified during English-to Japanese game localization.",
        "raw": "As we've seen, English words appear all the time in Japanese games.\nOver the years, these English words have formed a limited \"English\ngame vocabulary\" that Japanese gamers naturally absorb. However,\nit's still common for English phrases to be simplified during English-to\nJapanese game localization.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.11849082,
          0.11685714,
          0.6520532,
          0.19427857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11644027,
          0.11614286,
          0.6783002,
          0.19535
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "前面已经看到，日本游戏中经常出现英语词。多年来，它们形成了一套范围有限的“游戏英语词汇”，日本玩家玩着玩着就熟悉了。不过，英语游戏本地化成日语时，简化英文措辞仍然十分常见。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
