    {
      "id": "p0149-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The reverse of this practice can happen too. Sometimes overly simplified English text in a Japanese game will be rewritten with more complicated English during the Japanese-to-English localization process.",
        "raw": "The reverse of this practice can happen too. Sometimes overly simplified\nEnglish text in a Japanese game will be rewritten with more complicated\nEnglish during the Japanese-to-English localization process.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.11897269,
          0.5785,
          0.67624965,
          0.62285714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11644027,
          0.57778571,
          0.6783002,
          0.62392857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          11,
          12,
          13
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "反过来的情况也会发生。日本游戏中有时会出现过分简化的英语，日译英本地化时，又会把它们改写成更复杂的英语。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
